# {name}

Say here how to use {name} well: which operation to call first, what to store and what to do when it fails. Apps read this with
`jadpo package show {snake} --guide`.

## Before you release it

Delete this section when these are done.

1. Replace the `.example` hosts in `provider.jadpo`, the `account` resource, its types and the `read_account` recipe with your own. `jadpo package check` runs the
   publishing bar on the package whenever you want to know where it stands.
2. Confirm your operations against the API's sandbox with `jadpo package
   record`, which the registry shows as the package's contract.
3. Say what the package does in `package.jadpo`'s description, and why it is
   released in `CHANGELOG.md`.
4. To publish it to the public registry, choose an open licence in
   `package.jadpo` and name your handle as `publisher:`. A package only used
   by path or from git may stay `Licence.proprietary`, with no publisher.
5. Commit it, run `jadpo package check` and tag the commit `v1.0.0`.
